@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-header-is-one-row
Card reading MUST remain full screen. Its fixed header MUST have a 44dp cross,
a centered raised title pill occupying the available middle width, and a 44dp
vertical overflow menu. It MUST NOT add a second metadata row. Long titles may
ellipsize to one line in this pill, while keeping the complete title in text
semantics. The pill and controls MUST remain separate at narrow widths and large
font settings. Sheet headers remain plain titles; this pill belongs to the reader.
Source: Tavi's attached toolbar reference and one-row requirement, 22 October 2026.
